14ek|v|To deprive of life, animal or vegetable, in any manner or by any means; to render inanimate; to put to death; to slay. ; To destroy; to ruin; as, to kill one's chances; to kill the sale of a book. ; To cause to cease; to quell; to calm; to still; as, in seamen's language, a shower of rain kills the wind. ; To destroy the effect of; to counteract; to neutralize; as, alkali kills acid.	o:3qw,28,3;1hgk,2,3~3qw,28,3;1hgk,2,3	d:mtw,32,3;1loz,25,6;x5,17,3;1431,7,5~1loz,25,6;1431,7,5;mtw,32,3;x5,17,3
